<title>AUSTRIA: Saudis, Iran welcome OPEC accord.</title>
<headline>Saudis, Iran welcome OPEC accord.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabian Oil Minister Ali Nuaimi welcomed OPEC's decision on Thursday to freeze output quotas for six months as an &quot;excellent&quot; move.</p>
<p>Saudi Arabia is the biggest producer in the Organisation of the Petroleum Exporting Countries which has decided to continue with a production ceiling set at 25.03 million barrels daily.</p>
<p>Oil Minister Gholamreza Aqazadeh of Iran, the second biggest, told reporters that &quot;I am satisfied with the ceiling&quot;.</p>
<p>In other reactions, Kuwaiti Oil Minister Isa al-Mazeedi said he thought the OPEC accord would keep prices strong and perhaps move them somewhat higher.</p>
<p>&quot;I see no reason why prices should not stay the same, if not a bit higher,&quot; he said</p>
<p>He said he was not worried about resumed Iraqi sales as they would involve &quot;a very insignificant amount of oil&quot;.</p>
<p>The minister said OPEC ministers had looked at oil demand forecasts that showed the world economies &quot;really growing&quot;.</p>
</text>
